 col←readChildElements(vector type_id data count);_validity;nullmask
⍝ Read elements from a child vector based on type
⍝ vector: the DuckDB vector pointer
⍝ type_id: the type ID of the elements
⍝ data: pointer to the element data
⍝ count: number of elements
⍝ Returns: vector of elements

⎕io←0

_validity←api.duckdb_vector_get_validity vector

:Select type_id
:Case 1  ⍝ BOOLEAN
    col←count read.i8 data
:Case 2  ⍝ TINYINT
    col←count read.i8 data
:Case 3  ⍝ SMALLINT
    col←count read.i16 data
:Case 4  ⍝ INTEGER
    col←count read.i32 data
:Case 5  ⍝ BIGINT
    col←count read.i64 data
:Case 6  ⍝ UTINYINT
    col←count read.u8 data
:Case 7  ⍝ USMALLINT
    col←count read.u16 data
:Case 8  ⍝ UINTEGER
    col←count read.u32 data
:Case 9  ⍝ UBIGINT
    col←count read.u64 data
:Case 10  ⍝ FLOAT
    col←count read.float data
:Case 11  ⍝ DOUBLE
    col←count read.double data
:CaseList 17 28  ⍝ VARCHAR/JSON
    col←readStringElements data count
:case 25 ⍝ STRUCT
    col←readStructColumn vector data count
:Else
    ⎕←'Unsupported child type: ',⍕type_id
    col←count⍴⊂''
:EndSelect

⍝ Handle NULL values if validity mask exists
:If (_validity≢0)∧(count>0)
    nullmask←count↑{,⌽⍵ 8⍴11 ⎕DR ⍵ read.i8 _validity}⌈count÷8
    :Trap 0
        ((~nullmask)/col)←null
    :Else
        col←count⍴null
    :EndTrap
:EndIf

⍝ KSL 2.0.0
